(text "PRELIMINARY - R2 BLOCKED - NOT FOR FABRICATION. Values marked DATASHEET / ASSUMED in properties; calculations in Gate1d/Gate2 evidence.\nPOWER: Q301 drain=raw; Q302 drain=protected; common sources=PROT_MID=LTC7001 TS. No bypass. Eight raw bulk capacitors are UPSTREAM.\nCROWBAR: protected -> (R308+R309)||(R310+R311) -> Q303 drain; source=GND. Four33mOhm elements give33mOhm. Gate1d pulse conditions apply.\nARM: reset first; wait SUPPLY_OK/reference delay; press ARM. Delayed history latch prevents startup crowbar pulse; RUN requires both latches.\nFAULT: OV or loss of BUCK_PGOOD clears run latch; history holds; crowbar and input SHDN assert until RESET. No automatic retry.\nOPEN: timing/ringing,125C pulse thermal screen,<=220uF downstream sensitivity,series-FET SOA,inrush/bulk stability,actual harness resistance.\nCALCULATED: nominal trip5.325V; fault screen5.4816V (+18.39mV); Pi static5A4.7614V (+11.43mV). Neither margin is physically validated.\nCORRECTIONS: drain ballast; common-source pair;2.2Meg gate bleed preserves LTC charge pump;7.5V independent drive; clamp to sinking2.5V reference.\nCAPTURE CORRECTIONS: U315 pins1..6=VDD,OUTH,OUTL,GND,IN-,IN+; D303 isolates AUX against negative input; DRV_7V5 nominal7.623V.\nDATASHEET packages: DCT latch land; PCH bulk10x16mm; series FET footprints retain pins1..8. All MPN-OPEN passives require procurement review.\nERC source declarations: VIN_AUX via D303; VOUT_PROTECTED via the fitted opposed-FET channels. Flags do not bypass or validate protection." (at 15.24 457.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5588c4a8-c24c-5c3b-ab67-5800bf7c2ef2")) )
